erver is active, open your web browser and navigate to <a class="group inline" href="http://localhost:8787/fp" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><code>localhost:8787/fp</code><span class="whitespace-nowrap no-underline"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="ml-1 inline-block size-3.5! shrink-0 align-[-0.125em]"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 0h14v14H0z" opacity="0.2"></path><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" d="M9.915 8.885V4.08H5.11M9.625 4.375 4.083 9.917"></path></svg></span></a>.</p><p>Within the playground, you&#x27;ll find a visual exploration of your API. It reads your <code>/openapi.json</code> spec (generated by <code>hono-openapi</code> if enabled) to display all your defined API endpoints, such as <code>/api/tasks</code> or <code>/api/tasks/{id}</code>, within a user-friendly interface. This allows for easy request crafting; you can select an endpoint and fill in necessary parameters, path variables, and request bodies directly within the UI.</p><p>This is incredibly useful for quick testing and debugging cycles during development, reducing the frequent need for external tools like Postman or cURL.</p><p><span aria-owns="rmiz-modal-" data-rmiz=""><span data-rmiz-content="not-found" style="visibility:visible"><img alt="Fiberplane API Playground showing API endpoints for the HONC Task API" loading="lazy" width="704" height="447" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="" style="color:transparent;width:100%;height:100%" src="/docs/guides/honc-fiberplane-api-playground.png?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7"/></span></span></p></div></div></div></li><li class="numbered-step relative mt-8! mb-0! flex w-full items-start gap-4 pl-0! before:flex before:size-7 before:items-center before:justify-center before:rounded-full before:bg-gray-new-20 before:text-center before:font-mono before:text-sm before:leading-snug before:font-medium before:tracking-tight before:text-white before:content-[counter(section)] before:[counter-increment:section] after:absolute after:top-8 after:-bottom-7 after:left-[.8125rem] after:w-px after:bg-gray-new-90 first:mt-0! last:after:bottom-0 dark:before:bg-gray-new-90 dark:before:text-black-pure dark:after:bg-gray-new-30 [&amp;_h2]:text-2xl [&amp;_ol]:list-decimal!"><div class="w-[calc(100%-100px)] flex-1 [&amp;&gt;*_*:last-child]:mb-0 [&amp;&gt;*:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;*:first-child]:pt-0 md:[&amp;&gt;*:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;*:last-child]:mb-0"><h2 id="deploy-to-cloudflare-workers" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter"><span>Deploy to Cloudflare Workers</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#deploy-to-cloudflare-workers" aria-label="Link to Deploy to Cloudflare Workers"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h2><p>Deploy your application globally via Cloudflare&#x27;s edge network.</p><ol>
<li>
